            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Remaceras are mysterious fey who represent the natural cycle of transformative rebirth and metamorphosis. They believe that the cycle of reincarnation is the greatest expression of rebirth and revel in opportunities to send other creatures down this path. To a remacera, acts of violence are akin to scavengers and bacteria helping dead organisms decompose—and there may be some truth to this, as it isn't uncommon to find strange blossoms and fruits in their wake.</p>\n<p>Remaceras take the form of enormous caterpillars with striking patterns and serene human faces. Their calm visages are shattered when they stretch their jaws unnaturally wide to reveal a mouthful of deadly, sharklike teeth, which vibrate at high frequencies to damage and disorient foes. The most ancient remaceras can grow as long as 13 feet and weigh thousands of pounds.</p>\n<p>Despite their violent proclivities, remaceras savor the opportunity to have profound conversations with intelligent creatures. They seldom hold those who slay them in contempt, for they too receive renewal in death. Those who undergo a crisis of belief and turn nihilistic return as escorites.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
